!! Writing a normal "Hello World" is a bit boring, so lets try to itterate over the letters to print them.

!! The boiler starts of with 10L of water.
!! We are going to simply use all of it for this example.

coal 40


high_pressure_switch 200 !! Waiting for at least 20 bar.

set_put 10
press

set_put '!'
press

set_put 'm'
press
 
set_put 'a'
press

set_put 'e'
press

set_put 't'
press

set_put 'S'
press

set_put ' '
press

set_put 'o'
press

set_put 'l'
press
press

set_put 'e'
press

set_put 'H'
press

!! We pushed 13 characters onto the stack.
!! The write instruction costs 2 bar, move belt costs 1 bar per move.
!! The move instruction gets skipped when steam is less than 1 bar.

!! This leaves us with 4 bar per character, which is 52 bar.
!! The last character costs us 2 bar less because we skip the move instruction.
!! This brings us to 50 bar.

pump 10
coal 50
pump 25

release_valve 1
low_pressure_switch 502 !! 50.2 bar, 0.1 for setting the switch (release valve is opened!), 0.1 accounting for rounding errors.
release_valve 0

set_write_chr
press !! 2 bar

move_belt -2 !! 2 bar if not skipped.

!! Now you saw how conditional loops could be implemented. 
!! This is a simple example, because our character amount doesn't require a lot of pressure,
!! if we would have more characters, we would have to come up with a way to generate steam inside the loop
!! or load it from containers. Keep in mind: max pressure is 150bar.